 # Sessions
 
 For whoever changes login or the session expiry, or answers a member who was logged out. A session keeps a member
-logged in until 30 minutes pass without a request. The limit was 10 minutes until 2024, when members on slow mobile
-connections were logged out mid-checkout and lost their pantry orders.
+logged in between requests using a signed cookie. Slow mobile checkout prompted the current lifetime; a later
+database disk incident prompted the [storage change](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md).
 
 ## Lifetime
 
-Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
+Each request renews the session for 30 minutes; see `EXPIRY_MINUTES` and `expires_at` in
+[larder/sessions.py](../../larder/sessions.py). Until March 2024 the limit
 was 10 minutes: members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile connection were logged out before they confirmed it
 and lost what they had picked, and support logged 120 tickets about it that month. The limit was raised to 30
 minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The cookie carries the member and expiry, signed with a key shared by all web servers. See `sign` and `verify` in
+[larder/sessions.py](../../larder/sessions.py) for the format and validation. The
+[storage decision](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md) explains why the session table was dropped.
+
+## Deployment key
+
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY` is supplied through deploy secrets. Keep the same key on every web server and across deploys
+so existing cookies remain valid. The implementation falls back to `dev-only` when the variable is absent; deploys
+must supply the shared secret.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A maintainer cannot revoke one member's session from the server before its cookie expires. Wait for expiry under
+  the [session lifetime](#lifetime); the team accepted this limit for the pantry.
+- Rotating the signing key logs everyone out. Rotate it only between pickups, as agreed in
+  [issue 63](../../notes/issue-63.md).
 
